  "rationale": "All five candidates are direct matches by trait_reported/trait_efo to late-onset Alzheimer's disease. Among the closest endpoint-aligned family, PGS000053 and PGS000054 come from the same disease-focused publication with the same construction (21 genome-wide significant variants) and basic covariates (age, sex) and report per-SD OR effect sizes; per the provided domain guidance for late-onset neurodegenerative diseases, when siblings share the familial late-onset Alzheimer endpoint and basic covariates, the materially stronger OR is preferred. PGS000054 reports a stronger OR per SD (1.73, 95% CI 1.57–1.93) than PGS000053 (OR 1.29, 95% CI 1.21–1.37), making it the best-supported choice from the visible evidence. Limitations: the strongest-method candidates here are still sparse (GWAS-hits or C+T with very low variant counts), PRS-comparable AUC/R2 are not reported for any candidate (PGS004918 reports only full-model AUROC; PGS000334 reports an R² that appears to be full-model/unspecified), and PGS000054 is evaluated in AMR (Hispanic/Latin American) rather than EUR, reducing certainty without an explicit target deployment ancestry."
}

